syntax:
To use a predicate, pass it as an argument to an STL algorithm. For a unary predicate (e.g., for std::find_if): 
std::find_if(begin, end, unary_predicate);
Where unary_predicate is a function, functor, or lambda with signature: bool(ConstType& element);
For a binary predicate (e.g., for std::sort): 
std::sort(begin, end, binary_predicate);
With signature: bool(ConstType& a, ConstType& b);
Implementation notes: Lambdas are compiled into closure objects, which the compiler may inline. Functors require the class to define operator(), and the compiler handles them as objects, potentially involving member function calls. Always ensure predicates are pure (no side effects) for optimal optimization.
